WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.336
-The Justice Department
effectively called

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.604
the President
of the United States

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.038
a criminal on Friday

00:00:06.038 --> 00:00:07.907
as Trump announced the departure
of his chief of staff.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.809
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:14.313
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:16.583
Trump is desperate
to talk about anything

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:18.350
other than
the growing legal problems

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:19.652
engulfing his presidency.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.620
And you can tell
because he's picking fights

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.456
with everyone
from France to China

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.524
to his own
former Secretary of State.

00:00:25.524 --> 00:00:27.326
He's like a feral raccoon

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:28.661
trapped in a corner
in the attic.

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:29.795
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:31.731
If he loses in 2020,
they're going to have to

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:34.066
chase him out
of the Oval Office with a broom.

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:36.269
"Go! Get on!
Get outta here!

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:38.204
Oh, no!
Now he's biting the broom!"

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.305
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.305 --> 00:00:42.275
On Saturday, for example,

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:44.143
he unleashed
an unhinged Twitter rant

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:46.179
about Connecticut
Senator Richard Blumenthal

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:48.081
and unveiled
a new nickname for him,

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:49.849
calling him "The Dick."

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:50.850
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.353
Wow.
He's getting angrier and lazier.

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:54.654
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:57.490
The guy's name is Richard
so you nicknamed him "The Dick"?

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.926
Go ahead.
Take the rest of the week off.

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:01.294
You nailed it.

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.728
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:05.297
Then Trump called his former
Secretary of State Rex Tillerson

00:01:05.297 --> 00:01:07.133
"dumb as a rock"
and "lazy as hell"

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.834
after Tillerson,
in a rare interview,

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:11.637
offered some brutal criticism
of his former boss.

00:01:11.637 --> 00:01:14.039
-How would you describe
Donald Trump?

00:01:14.039 --> 00:01:15.875
-He acts on his instincts.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:19.279
In some respects,
that looks like impulsiveness.

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:24.150
But it's not his intent
to act on impulse.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:27.520
I think he really is trying
to act on his instincts.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.824
It was challenging for me
coming from the disciplined,

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:35.260
highly process-oriented
ExxonMobil Corporation

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:40.499
to go to work for a man
who is pretty undisciplined,

00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:42.869
doesn't like to read.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.804
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.606
-That's the former
Secretary of State

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:49.442
talking about the
president of the United States

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.810
like he's Mowgli.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.411
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:56.081
"I mean, he doesn't mean to howl
and walk on all fours.

00:01:56.081 --> 00:01:58.184
He was raised by wolves."

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:59.418
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.418 --> 00:02:01.020
Although, in fairness to Trump,

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.788
the reason
he doesn't like to read

00:02:02.788 --> 00:02:06.726
is that he is bad at it,
even if he will never admit it.

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:10.730
-Through their lives,
and though their lives...

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:15.801
Beating expectations
in the House for the midtown

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.870
and midterm year.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:20.406
They sacrifice every day

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:23.710
for the furniture --
future of their children.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.310
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:27.913
-Instead of saying --

00:02:27.913 --> 00:02:30.683
Instead of saying, "furniture,
excuse me, future..."

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.051
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:35.455
He doubled down
on "furniture" and "future."

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:37.190
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:39.692
Can you imagine being this guy's
Secretary of State?

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.194
"I want to bomb North Dakota."

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:42.428
"You mean North Korea?"

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:44.731
"I mean North Dakota
and North Korea!"

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.366
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:48.868
"I meant both!
You cut me off!"

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:50.202
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.202 --> 00:02:52.672
"Before I got to North Korea."

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.607
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:57.343
And while he fires off one
Twitter insult after another,

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.011
his White House
is also undergoing

00:02:59.011 --> 00:03:00.847
an unprecedented level
of staff turnover.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:02.081
People are quitting
this White House

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:04.751
like it's a Kmart
the day before Black Friday.

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:06.051
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.051 --> 00:03:08.087
And on Saturday,
Trump confirmed speculation

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.421
that Chief of Staff John Kelly

00:03:09.421 --> 00:03:11.390
would be leaving the White House
at the end of the year,

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:14.727
which means we're at the end
of the John Kelly era.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:17.063
And I just hope that
now that his tenure is over,

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:20.399
everyone who hailed him as a
paragon of discipline and order

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:22.101
when he first took over
will look back and admit

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.437
that they were very wrong.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:27.373
-Kelly's mission is less drama,
more discipline

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.007
inside the inner circle.

00:03:29.007 --> 00:03:30.843
-He's gonna be great.

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:33.512
Keeping things organized,
keeping everyone in their lane.

00:03:33.512 --> 00:03:36.649
-I think he will
bring some order and discipline

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.083
to the West Wing.

00:03:38.083 --> 00:03:40.019
-I hope that he will demonstrate
to the president

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.554
the value of discipline.

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:44.990
-If anybody can bring order and
discipline to this White House,

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.459
it is General Kelly.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:49.362
I hope that we're
at a turning point now.

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:50.529
-Oh, hey,
it's Senator Richard Blumenthal

00:03:50.529 --> 00:03:51.898
from earlier.

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.265
And you were right, Senator --
it was a turning point.

00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:55.001
When it started,
you were Richard Blumenthal,

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:57.103
and when it ended,
you were "The Dick."

00:03:57.103 --> 00:04:01.808
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:03.576
Guess he stayed in his lane.

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:05.077
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:07.513
Kelly was never going to bring
discipline to this White House.

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:09.115
For one thing,
you can't change Trump.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:12.485
And, also, Kelly wanted
the same thing as Trump.

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.721
We all just projected ourselves
onto Kelly

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:17.356
because his face
always looked the way we felt.

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:18.791
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:21.927
But now we know
that's just his face.

00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:25.732
That's his "Everything
is going great" face.

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:28.701
Here he is, blowing out the
candles on his birthday cake.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.203
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:32.238
And here's John Kelly
on a roller coaster.

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:34.107
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:36.609
-In fact,
Kelly served a president

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.744
for whom lawbreaking
was apparently so routine

00:04:38.744 --> 00:04:41.680
that Tillerson had to routinely
explain to the President

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:44.050
that the things he wanted to do
were illegal.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.586
-When the President would say,
"Well, here's what I want to do,

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:48.687
and here's how I want to do it,"

00:04:48.687 --> 00:04:51.124
and I'd have to say to him,
"Well, Mr. President,

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:54.927
I understand what you want to do
but you can't do it that way.

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:57.896
It violates the law.
It violates treaty."

00:04:57.896 --> 00:05:00.099
-The Secretary of State
had to explain to the President

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:01.800
that what
he wanted to do was illegal.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:04.036
I can't even imagine
what that was.

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:06.038
"Yes, Mr. President,
we have the technology,

00:05:06.038 --> 00:05:07.773
but you can't
just shoot someone into space.

00:05:07.773 --> 00:05:09.876
It's illegal, and on top of
that, it's your son."

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:12.911
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.911 --> 00:05:15.181
Trump is fundamentally lawless.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.983
Not only does he think
he's above the law,

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:19.685
he doesn't even
understand the law.

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:21.520
And on Friday,
we got clearest picture yet

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.089
of his serial lawbreaking.

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:25.124
The Special Counsel
in the Russia investigation

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:27.727
and prosecutors in New York
filed sentencing memos

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:29.862
for Trump's ex-campaign chairman
Paul Manafort

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:31.631
and his ex-fixer Michael Cohen.

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:34.433
And they made it pretty clear
that the Justice Department

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:37.436
has damning evidence
on Trump's ties to Russia.

00:05:37.436 --> 00:05:39.939
-In a new court filing,
Special Counsel Robert Mueller

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:42.575
says former Trump campaign
chairman Paul Manafort

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:44.743
lied about several key points

00:05:44.743 --> 00:05:47.713
after agreeing
to cooperate with prosecutors.

00:05:47.713 --> 00:05:49.882
-Now, this could mean Mueller's
team has more evidence

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:52.584
about contacts between people
close the President

00:05:52.584 --> 00:05:55.754
and Russians
during the 2016 campaign.

00:05:55.754 --> 00:05:59.191
-In November 2015,
prosecutors say Cohen

00:05:59.191 --> 00:06:00.993
spoke with a Russian national

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:04.931
who claimed to be a trusted
person in the Russian Federation

00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:08.267
who promised the campaign
political synergy

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:11.003
and synergy
on a government level.

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:12.304
-Oh, synergy.

00:06:12.304 --> 00:06:15.107
Trump must have been so pumped
when he heard that.

00:06:15.107 --> 00:06:17.609
"See, it wasn't collusion.
It was synergy.

00:06:17.609 --> 00:06:21.380
And now I'm just
gonna check my thesaurus.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.948
And, son of a bitch!"

00:06:22.948 --> 00:06:25.485
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:25.485 --> 00:06:29.355
And -- And if you thought --

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:30.622
[ Applause ]

00:06:30.622 --> 00:06:32.858
If you thought prosecutors
were being coy

00:06:32.858 --> 00:06:35.227
when they used the word synergy
instead of collusion,

00:06:35.227 --> 00:06:36.562
they were much more on the nose

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:38.764
in their sentencing
recommendations for Cohen.

00:06:38.764 --> 00:06:41.033
Prosecutors spelled out
as clearly as possible

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:42.267
in this document
that they believe

00:06:42.267 --> 00:06:43.736
the President
of the United States

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:46.905
committed a crime by paying
hush money to cover up affairs.

00:06:46.905 --> 00:06:48.040
How do we know that?

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.842
Well, they didn't
mention Trump by name,

00:06:49.842 --> 00:06:51.310
but according
to the court documents,

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:54.313
"During the campaign,
Cohen played a central role

00:06:54.313 --> 00:06:57.383
in two similar schemes to
purchase the rights to stories,

00:06:57.383 --> 00:07:00.086
each from women
who'd claimed to have an affair

00:07:00.086 --> 00:07:02.954
with Individual 1,
so as to suppress the stories

00:07:02.954 --> 00:07:05.691
and thereby prevent them
from influencing the election."

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:07.159
And who is Individual 1?

00:07:07.159 --> 00:07:09.661
Well, the court documents are
cryptic, but here's one clue.

00:07:09.661 --> 00:07:13.399
"On approximately June 16, 2015,
Individual 1 began

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:15.434
an ultimately
successful campaign

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:17.336
for President of
the United States."

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:20.106
[ Laughter ]

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:22.909
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:32.484
[ Laughter ]

00:07:32.484 --> 00:07:37.690
Of course,
the only thing worse for Trump

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.791
than finding out
he's Individual 1

00:07:39.791 --> 00:07:42.828
would be if he found out
he was Individual 2.

00:07:42.828 --> 00:07:43.930
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:45.831
"Who the hell is number 1?!"

00:07:45.831 --> 00:07:47.032
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.032 --> 00:07:49.668
"It's not Hillary, is it?"

00:07:49.668 --> 00:07:50.969
So there you go --
the court documents

00:07:50.969 --> 00:07:52.471
say explicitly
that Individual 1

00:07:52.471 --> 00:07:54.406
committed a felony,
and they made clear

00:07:54.406 --> 00:07:56.709
that Individual 1 is the
President of the United States,

00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:58.277
or as Trump put it on Twitter,

00:07:58.277 --> 00:08:00.112
"Totally clears the President,
thank you."

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:01.613
[ Laughter ]

00:08:01.613 --> 00:08:03.082
Now,
you might be asking yourself,

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:04.984
how could Trump
have read these documents

00:08:04.984 --> 00:08:07.219
and come to the conclusion
that they totally clear him?

00:08:07.219 --> 00:08:09.822
And he explained it
to reporters on Saturday.

00:08:09.822 --> 00:08:13.125
-On the Mueller situation,
we're very happy with

00:08:13.125 --> 00:08:14.626
what we are reading,

00:08:14.626 --> 00:08:17.896
because there was
no collusion whatsoever.

00:08:17.896 --> 00:08:20.433
I think it's all turning around
very nicely.

00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:24.136
But as far as the report
that we see,

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:25.871
according to everybody
I've spoken to --

00:08:25.871 --> 00:08:27.840
I have not read it.
-You --

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:29.208
[ Laughter ]

00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:31.210
You didn't read it?

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:33.679
Oh, dude, you --
you should read it.

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:35.414
[ Laughter ]

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:37.682
If there was a document
that detailed crimes

00:08:37.682 --> 00:08:40.620
I was implicated in,
the only way I wouldn't read it

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.755
is if I knew what was in it.

00:08:42.755 --> 00:08:45.824
Trump might as well
go full old cowboy and say,

00:08:45.824 --> 00:08:48.227
"I don't have to read it, boy.

00:08:48.227 --> 00:08:49.462
I lived it."

00:08:49.462 --> 00:08:51.130
[ Laughter ]

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.265
Well, in lieu of reading,
Trump must've spent the weekend

00:08:53.265 --> 00:08:55.133
psyching himself up,
because this morning,

00:08:55.133 --> 00:08:56.435
he got up early and gave us all

00:08:56.435 --> 00:08:58.371
that classic Twitter meltdown
we were expecting.

00:08:58.371 --> 00:08:59.872
And aside from the misspellings,

00:08:59.872 --> 00:09:01.873
watch how many times
he changes his argument

00:09:01.873 --> 00:09:03.442
in the span of just two tweets.

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:05.277
-Democrats can't find
a smoking gun

00:09:05.277 --> 00:09:06.812
tying the Trump campaign
to Russia

00:09:06.812 --> 00:09:08.680
after James Comey's testimony.

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:11.884
No smoking gun, no collusion.
@FoxNews

00:09:11.884 --> 00:09:15.221
That's because there was," all
caps, "no collusion.

00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:17.590
So now the Dems go to simple
private transaction,

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:19.691
wrongly calling it
a campaign contribution,

00:09:19.691 --> 00:09:22.761
which it was not,
but even if it was,

00:09:22.761 --> 00:09:25.564
it's only a civil case,
like Obama's.

00:09:25.564 --> 00:09:27.632
But it was done correctly
by a lawyer,

00:09:27.632 --> 00:09:29.769
and there would not even
be a fine.

00:09:29.769 --> 00:09:33.139
Lawyer's liability
if he made a mistake, not me.

00:09:33.139 --> 00:09:35.708
Cohen," speaking of
Michael Cohen, his former fixer,

00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:38.010
"just trying to get
his sentence reduced."

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.579
All caps, "Witch hunt!"

00:09:40.579 --> 00:09:44.483
-My God. It was legal,
but if it wasn't, it was civil.

00:09:44.483 --> 00:09:45.884
But it was done correctly,

00:09:45.884 --> 00:09:47.720
but if it wasn't,
it's not my fault."

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:49.054
[ Laughter ]

00:09:49.054 --> 00:09:51.590
But to put it a way Donald Trump
will understand,

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:53.825
where there's smock,
there's foyer.

00:09:53.825 --> 00:09:57.162
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:57.162 --> 00:10:02.367
And let's just --

00:10:02.367 --> 00:10:04.036
let's just address for a second

00:10:04.036 --> 00:10:06.205
this argument that Obama
did the same thing,

00:10:06.205 --> 00:10:07.839
because it's an argument
Trump's supporters

00:10:07.839 --> 00:10:09.441
are starting to make,
and it's insane.

00:10:09.441 --> 00:10:11.143
Every campaign
makes paperwork errors.

00:10:11.143 --> 00:10:12.244
That happens all the time.

00:10:12.244 --> 00:10:15.081
And in 2013,
Obama's campaign was fined

00:10:15.081 --> 00:10:16.615
for omitting some donors' names.

00:10:16.615 --> 00:10:19.118
Independent experts called it
relatively minor,

00:10:19.118 --> 00:10:20.252
and even a Republican lawyer

00:10:20.252 --> 00:10:22.087
said it was
a very clean audit report

00:10:22.087 --> 00:10:23.422
for the Obama campaign.

00:10:23.422 --> 00:10:25.190
And let's be honest,
there's a huge difference

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:27.525
between an accounting error
and a hush payment

00:10:27.525 --> 00:10:29.228
to cover up an affair.

00:10:29.228 --> 00:10:31.230
If you don't believe me,
go home and tell your spouse,

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:34.467
"I had sex with a porn star
and made an accounting error."

00:10:34.467 --> 00:10:35.534
[ Laughter ]

00:10:35.534 --> 00:10:37.902
Let me know which one
they focus on.

00:10:37.902 --> 00:10:42.908
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:42.908 --> 00:10:45.478
Trump didn't just
make a paperwork error.

00:10:45.478 --> 00:10:47.646
It's not like he was sitting
there with a green eye shade,

00:10:47.646 --> 00:10:50.148
trying to balance the books
and missed something.

00:10:50.148 --> 00:10:52.484
"Let's see --
50 bucks for pizza,

00:10:52.484 --> 00:10:54.820
$100 for lawn signs.

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:57.156
Oh, $130,000
to pay off a porn star.

00:10:57.156 --> 00:10:59.091
I almost forgot.
I'll put that under utilities."

00:10:59.091 --> 00:11:00.726
[ Laughter ]

00:11:00.726 --> 00:11:02.394
Every day,
there are new revelations

00:11:02.394 --> 00:11:05.030
that seem to fade away,
but this feels like a watershed.

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:06.232
The Justice Department
just called

00:11:06.232 --> 00:11:07.899
the President of
the United States a criminal.

00:11:07.899 --> 00:11:09.835
I don't know if Trump will
ever be indicted or impeached,

00:11:09.835 --> 00:11:12.304
but if he is, he probably won't
know what he's charged with

00:11:12.304 --> 00:11:15.006
because he --
-Doesn't like to read.

00:11:15.006 --> 00:11:16.508
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:16.508 --> 00:11:20.413
[ Cheers and applause ]

